<title>UK: Littlewoods may sell 19 stores-paper.</title>
<headline>Littlewoods may sell 19 stores-paper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's privately-owned retail to football pools group Littlewoods is in talks to sell 19 of its largest stores to a single buyer for about 120 million pounds, the Times newspaper said on Monday.</p>
<p>It said the sale could be agreed as early as this week and added the company had been in talks with Boots Co Plc, Next Plc and Marks and Spencer Plc.</p>
<p>Two weeks ago Littlewoods abandoned plans to sell its retail chain and said it would refocus strategy while selling off selected sites. -- London newsroom 44 171 542 7947</p>
